{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionClassForcesComplexType","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionClassForcesComplexType","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Group","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.TypeTags.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.obs_neg_of_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.obs_neg_of_inv","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L181-L193","doc":"**The `μ₃ ≅ ZMod 3` bridge.**  `cocycle_dual` says the dual lift's cocycle is the\n*inverse*; `obs_dual` says the class *negates*.  Transporting along an isomorphism of the\ncentre with `Multiplicative (ZMod 3)` is what turns one into the other — inversion in the\ngroup is negation in `ZMod 3`.\n\nWith this, the algebraic chain behind `obs_dual` is complete: inverse-transpose is a\nhomomorphism (`cocycle_map`), it inverts the centre (`cocycle_dual`), and inversion of a\n`μ₃` value is negation of a `ZMod 3` value (here).  What is still missing for a genuine\n`instance` is only the passage from a *cocycle* to its *cohomology class* — H² machinery\n— and the relative-vs-absolute step, which is checked computationally instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_conj_of_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_conj_of_comm","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L174-L179","doc":"**`obs_congr`, as group theory.**  A cocycle commuting with the conjugator — which\ncentrality supplies — is unchanged by conjugating the lift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_conj","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L168-L172","doc":"Conjugating a lift conjugates its cocycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_dual","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L161-L166","doc":"**`obs_dual`, as group theory.**  If `φ` inverts the cocycle's value — as\ninverse-transpose does on the centre — then the dual lift's cocycle is the inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.cocycle_map","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L156-L159","doc":"A homomorphism applied to a lift carries its cocycle along. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.cocycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.cocycle","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L153-L154","doc":"The failure of a set-theoretic lift `s` to be multiplicative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.not_selfDual_of_obs_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.not_selfDual_of_obs_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L119-L123","doc":"**The form a search uses.**  Every representation in a non-trivial obstruction class\nfails to be self-dual — hence is of complex type, with no variety decomposition required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.obs_eq_zero_of_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.obs_eq_zero_of_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L114-L117","doc":"A self-dual representation has trivial obstruction class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality.obs_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality.obs_congr","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L110-L110","doc":"The obstruction class is an isomorphism invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality.obs_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality.obs_dual","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L108-L108","doc":"Duality negates the obstruction class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ObstructionDuality","kind":"class","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L101-L110","doc":"The two topological inputs, named so the theorem below wears what it uses.\n\n`obs` is the obstruction class to lifting a boundary-unipotent `PGL(3,ℂ)` representation\nto `SL(3,ℂ)`; `dual` is `ρ ↦ ᵗρ⁻¹`; `Iso` is isomorphism of representations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.eq_zero_of_eq_neg_zmod_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.eq_zero_of_eq_neg_zmod_three","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L94-L99","doc":"The `ℤ/3` case used by the obstruction argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.eq_zero_of_add_self_eq_zero_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.eq_zero_of_add_self_eq_zero_odd","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ObstructionClassForcesComplexType.lean#L78-L92","doc":"In `ZMod n` with `n = 2m+1` odd, `x + x = 0` forces `x = 0`: `2` is invertible. ","signatureChunk":0}]}